From 80607fdb819198b629b89b26e3bb3146367c05a4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Henri Sundelin <henris42@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 20:07:46 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Data races between the loader threads and the main
 thread, a use-after-free at exit, and smaller faults

Found with address- and thread-sanitizer builds running a host program
(a glTF scene of about 60 files loaded through async_load_url, drawn with
execute_ml). Before: 45 kinds of race reported per start and a
heap-use-after-free in InstallProgress in one run of three. After: none
in the engine.

Races
- InstallProgress, ProgressBar, SetTicks, FindProgressVal/Max, SetupProgress,
  ClearProgress: the progress lists were pushed to by loader threads and the
  main thread at once. One recursive mutex around them.
- add_async_cb / rem_async_cb: the callback list, the same way.
- Task queue: wait_for_push_or_shutdown read the queue under `mutex` while
  it is changed under `queue_mutex`. Lock order is now mutex, then
  queue_mutex; push_to_queue signals after it has let go of queue_mutex.
  tasks_async_join_m and tasks_done_queue_clear take queue_mutex.
- g_current_size / g_total_size (std::map written by several loaders).
- del_map::async_get2 used its list entry after unlocking.
- g_del_map_deleter_installed, thread_counter, task_num: atomic.
- GltfMeshAllP::FacePoint (both classes): the one-entry cache was shared by
  the threads that copy one mesh in parallel, which could hand out a torn
  point. The cache is per thread now.
- LoadGltf::PrePrepare could run on the loader thread and the main thread
  at once.
- g_copy_progress was incremented by every copying thread for each face and
  read by nobody; the increment is gone.

Memory
- VertexArraySet: a copy followed a pointer to its original in its
  destructor; at exit (Rest::~Rest) the original was already deleted. The
  original and its copies now share an owner that deletes the Polys once,
  whatever the order.
- load_urls2: when two tasks loaded one url at the same time, the second
  result replaced the first and the first buffer was lost. The first stays,
  the second is freed.
- thread_func_gltf_bitmap: the downscale of images over 512 px used the
  height as the length of a row and wrote 4 bytes per pixel whatever the
  format: out of bounds for an image taller than wide.

Other
- ASyncLoader::get_loaded_data added the "load_url.php?url=" prefix to the
  url on every pass of its retry loop, so only the first pass could match.
- fetch_2_success (Emscripten): the loop over g_pending_fetch ran to the
  size of another list, so finished urls stayed marked as pending.
- Makefile: `ifeq (DEBUG,address)` compared two constants;
  `make DEBUG=address` now turns the address sanitizer on.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
